                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "'Luxor Amun Rising' classic Egyptian-themed marble-shooter puzzle games where you control a winged scarab to fire colored spheres and eliminate advancing chains before they reach the pyramids.\n\nIt's nostalgic, simple, and incredibly addictive. There's a great stage variety, and satisfying power-ups. Although I'm not sure whether I have ever played this one; because both 'Luxor' and 'Luxor Amun Rising' are almost the same game. Factually, it's the real 'Luxor 2', but technically, it's more like 'Luxor 1.5'; the only difference is that this is aimed more towards veteran players, because it's slightly harder than 'Luxor'.\n\nMy only problem with this game is that the devs abandoned it and didn't renew the files for newer systems; since Flash was discontinued, so did these retro games that were based on Flash.",
